# user can select a topo here or in GUI (json sidecar file)
# planner auto selects to detour congestion/obstacles
#
# NOTE (hanan_loci default flip): this healer-less R&D flow's endpoint shifted
# from 0 overlaps / 0 opens to 1 overlap / 16 dnuts-unplaced — the UNPINNED
# bundles (1, 3) now auto-select loci candidates.  No test or doc pins the old
# endpoint, so the flow deliberately stays on the default pool; opt out with
# `generate_topologies no_hanan_loci` to reproduce the pre-flip endpoint.

source tracks/tracks2top.buda
add_block drv1    50  380  230  620
add_block rcv1   680  120  880  500
add_block rcv2   350   50  550  230

add_bus a[16] drv1.o rcv1.i,rcv2.i
add_bus b[16] rcv1.o drv1.i,rcv2.i
add_bus c[16] rcv2.o drv1.i,rcv1.i

run_bundler strict
generate_topologies
visualize_topologies

# force bundle 3 to switch to another topo:
add_keepout 600 250 650 350 M6

#in json:
#select_topology 1 3

# TRUNK_V+MST@x290; index 9 since the hanan_loci default flip grew the pool
# 26->38 (same candidate by topo_uid, was index 4).
select_topology 2 9

#planner selects topo 1 without keepout:
#select_topology 3 1

#[Planner] Bundle 1 (24 units wide) -> topo 3 of 14: TRUNK_H@y175 [pinned]  [H→M6 V→M5]  overflow=0
#[Planner] Bundle 2 (24 units wide) -> topo 4 of 14: TRUNK_H@y440 [pinned]  [H→M6 V→M5]  overflow=0
#[Planner] Bundle 3 (24 units wide) -> topo 2 of 14: TRUNK_V@x450  [V→M5 H→M6 H→M6]  overflow=16

run_planner

run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
visualize
